So I was doing the barbarian quest (mostly to kill time while I wait for
something better then Cleaver (and Werebane doesn't count, dammit Set!))
and found a 'trice in one of the cave rooms.  I killed it, picked up the
corpse, and thought "If I dug down, I could probably find Thoth Amon
quickly and end this whole thing!"  But I took the careful route...until
an Ogre zapped a hole in the ground with a wand of digging.

I took one look at the hole, and then jumped in!

I didn't have too much trouble reaching Thoth Amon (left a stone menagerie
in my wake), got up close to him (had Stealth) and killed him with the
cockatrice corpse!  Granted, I had to beat him to death with it - what's
with this big purple @ being stoning resistant?

It's very satisfying being able to beat my quest nemesis to a bloody pulp
with what amounts to a real rubber chicken.  I never even lost that many
hit points.  W00t barbarians!

I had been thinking of trying to tame the 4 dragons in the Castle, but
now...damn, I don't need them!

